Consider the following Python code snippet. A={"this","that"}
    B={"that","other"}
    C={"other","this"}
    while "other" in C:
        if "this" in A:
            A,B,C=A-B,B-C,C-A
        if "that" in B:
            A,B,C=C|A,A|B,B|C When the above program is executed, at the end, which of the following sets contains "this"?

Consider the following Python code snippet. def f(a,b):
        if (a==0):
            return b
        if (a%2==1):
            return 2*f((a-1)/2,b)
        return b+f(a-1,b)
    print(f(15,10)) The value printed by the code snippet is _________ (Answer in integer)

Consider the following pseudocode. Create empty stack S
    Set x=0, flag=0, sum=0
    Push x onto S
    while (S is not empty){
        if (flag equals 0){
            Set x = x+1
            Push x onto S}
        if (x equals 8):
            Set flag=1
        if (flag equals 1){
            x = Pop(S)
            if (x is odd):
                Pop(S)
            Set sum = sum + x}
    }
    Output sum The value of sum output by a program executing the above pseudocode is ___________ (Answer in integer)
